+        </dd>
+        <dt pn="section-3-3.3">AUTHENTICATION/SECURITY DATA (ADAT)</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-3-3.4">
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-3-3.4.1">The argument field is a Telnet string representing base 64 encoded
+security data (see Section 9, &quot;Base 64 Encoding&quot;).  If a reply
+code indicating success is returned, the server may also use a
+string of the form &quot;ADAT=base64data&quot; as the text part of the reply
+if it wishes to convey security data back to the client.</t>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-3-3.4.2">The data in both cases is specific to the security mechanism
